# Chad's Personal Knowledge Base

This file is the single source of truth for what Chad knows about you.
Edit it freely — plain English. Chad re-syncs it on every startup, so added,
edited, and deleted lines all take effect on restart.

Copy this file to `config/personal_knowledge.md` and fill it in.
That file is gitignored — your data stays local.

### How it works

**Write one fact per line.** Each line under a `## section` becomes its own fact in
the knowledge graph, retrieved and scored on its own. Don't write a paragraph — a
whole section stored as one lump gets truncated when injected, and the truncator
decides which of your facts survives.

Three headings are reserved:

| Heading | What it's for |
|---|---|
| `## _core_profile` | Who you are. Injected into every prompt verbatim, never retrieved. |
| `## _behavior` | How Chad should act. Also always on, never retrieved. |
| `## _graph` | Typed people/places/events Chad can walk at query time. |

Everything else is a normal topic section of retrievable facts.

---

## _core_profile

[The handful of facts that matter on almost any turn. This block is injected into
every prompt verbatim — it is never retrieved, so it can never be ranked out or
truncated away. Everything else in this file reaches Chad through similarity
search, which is right for the long tail and wrong for "who do I live with".
Keep it under ~800 characters and boring: name, where you live, who you live with,
what you do, what's coming up. Not your height. If Chad ever asks you to
re-explain something basic about your own life, that fact belongs here.]

## _behavior

[Standing directives about how Chad should ACT — not facts about you. Also always
on, also never retrieved: as ordinary facts these matched weakly against almost
any query and leaked into unrelated turns.
e.g. "Ask clarifying questions with the ask_user_question tool, not in chat."
e.g. "Prefer recent emails; don't resurface year-old todos as current."]

